From: AeroGauge Contributors <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] recompinput: skip already-registered devices on SDL_CONTROLLERDEVICEADDED

During startup, SDL2-compat / SDL3 can emit SDL_CONTROLLERDEVICEADDED for a
hotplug concurrently with the host's startup controller enumeration. Checking
recompinput::get_controller_from_joystick_id before calling SDL_GameControllerOpen
prevents opening a second SDL_GameController handle for the same instance ID.

diff --git a/recompinput/src/input_events.cpp b/recompinput/src/input_events.cpp
index d839d12..1000001 100644
--- a/recompinput/src/input_events.cpp
+++ b/recompinput/src/input_events.cpp
@@ -73,6 +73,10 @@ bool sdl_event_filter(void* userdata, SDL_Event* event) {
     case SDL_EventType::SDL_CONTROLLERDEVICEADDED:
     {
         SDL_ControllerDeviceEvent* controller_event = &event->cdevice;
+        const SDL_JoystickID instance_id = SDL_JoystickGetDeviceInstanceID(controller_event->which);
+        if (instance_id != -1 && recompinput::get_controller_from_joystick_id(instance_id) != nullptr) {
+            break;
+        }
         SDL_GameController* controller = SDL_GameControllerOpen(controller_event->which);
         printf("Controller added: %d\n", controller_event->which);
         if (controller != nullptr) {
